ey had the trapped or at  the beginning of the experiment they  could easily tell whether they received  a superposition or a single measured  pre-image by just applying the Fourier  transform and distinguishing lwe from  uniform using the trapdoor but in our  experiment we first asked the adversary  to show us a pre-image and then if we're  convinced that it's correct we can  reveal a trapdoor and in some sense the  adversary cannot go back and tell  whether it initially received a  superposition or a single measured  pre-image okay so in other words we want  to claim that the only way a can obtain  a certificate Pi is by measuring the  state in the computational basis okay  and we know that if the adversary does  this then B is hidden once and for all  because it was in the phase and it's  erased okay now unfortunately unlike the  standard gaussian collapse in property  which I can prove under lwe the strong  gaussian collapsing property is much  more difficult to prove I made some  progress towards it in the paper and I  describe some general bottlenecks  but assuming this conjecture we get  public key encryption schemes and  homomorphic encryption schemes with  certified deletion and public  verification using a very simple  template so one open problem is to  actually prove this conjecture using  similar assumptions like LW or sis  okay so this brings me to the end of my  talk so I just want to highlight a quick  summary of the contributions so I  presented the first non-hi non-hybrid  approach for certified deletion schemes  that uses kind of quantum superpositions  of lwe samples and a nice side effect as  I mentioned is that you get public  verification for free okay and in  previous work this was only possible  with very strong cryptographic  assumptions  and the second contribution is this idea  of gaussian collapsing which is kind of  a natural  um  notion of the itai hash function  especially in the context when working  with lwe and SAS  and then I gave two public encryption  schemes for certified deletion the Dual  reggae scheme and the Dual GSW scheme  that's actually homomorphic okay so I  want to end with two open problems so  one is to actually prove the strong  gaussian collapsing property under LW in  sis or the inhomogeneous sis version and  in the paper I made some progress  towards this and I explained kind of the  last bottlenecks and that one would have  to solve  and the second open problem is to  actually dequantize the communication  between a client and a server in the fhe  protocol with certified deletion okay so  almost everything is classical for  example we can classically verify  deletion certificates and so on but  it'll be nice if one could de-quantize  the remaining communication so that the  client and the quantum server can  interact using classical channels only  okay so this marks the end of my talk uh  I'm happy to receive questions by email  and I'm looking forward to the  conference thank you for your attention
 

